From 7f83e291a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini 3.6 Flash <gemini@google.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:58:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: Only attempt to map buffer objects with host visible memory.

In adapter_vk_alloc_bo(), wined3d allocates Vulkan buffer objects.
When creating GPU-only buffers (WINED3D_RTYPE_BUFFER) without host access
flags, memory_type is allocated as device-local without
VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT.

Unconditionally calling wined3d_bo_vk_map() on non-host-visible memory causes
vkMapMemory() to fail with VK_ERROR_MEMORY_MAP_FAILED (-5) and produces error
logs (ERR("Failed to map bo.\n")), causing buffer allocation to fail during
Direct3D backend initialization for applications like Kontakt 8.

Fix by checking that memory_type contains VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT
before calling wined3d_bo_vk_map().
---
 dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c b/dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c
index 55c7b167156..5661df0c102 100644
--- a/dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/adapter_vk.c
@@ -1223,7 +1223,7 @@ static bool adapter_vk_alloc_bo(struct wined3d_device *device, struct wined3d_re
         return false;
     }
 
-    if (!bo_vk->b.map_ptr)
+    if ((memory_type & VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT) && !bo_vk->b.map_ptr)
     {
         if (!wined3d_bo_vk_map(bo_vk, context_vk))
             ERR("Failed to map bo.\n");
-- 
2.43.0
